T6050 (M5 Pro/Max): propagate the SuperSpeed ATC PHY tunables into the DT.

m1n1 selects its ATC tunable table by the PHY's ADT compatible. T6050's
atc-phy,t6050 / atc-phy,t6040 matched none of the known branches, so it fell to
the oldest (t8103) table, whose tunable names the T6050 ADT does not have -
result: no SuperSpeed tunable reached Linux and the PHY could only do USB2.

Add an atc_tunables_t6050[] table for this generation, a compat branch to select
it, an empty-fuse entry (fuses are not required from t6020 on), and the cleanup
delprop. Sub-block offsets are by analogy to t8122 and range-checked against the
ADT triples; the three tunables whose sub-block base is still unknown are left
out (documented inline) rather than guessed, since a wrong base corrupts
registers. USB3 is the first target; USB4/Thunderbolt (CIO4PLL) follows.

Pairs with the atc.c atcphy_hw_t6050 generation (t6050-usb2-host.patch): that
config already drives the SuperSpeed engine once these tunables are present.

Not tested on hardware (the proxy was down). Apply from the omacom-m1n1 root:
    git apply kernel/usb2-host/t6050-usb4-m1n1-tunables.patch

--- a/src/kboot_atc.c
+++ b/src/kboot_atc.c
@@ -174,6 +174,40 @@
 };
 
 /*
+ * T6050 (M5 Pro/Max). A new PHY generation of the t8122 family: the AUSPLL sits
+ * at the same core offset, but the CIO PLL is "CIO4PLL" and the common/lane
+ * tunables are renamed and fewer. Sub-block offsets are by analogy to
+ * atc_tunables_t8122[] (fabric 0x44000, AUSPLL 0x2200, CIO PLL 0x2a00, lane0/1
+ * 0x9000/0x10000) and were range-checked against the ADT triples. T6050 has no
+ * USB/CIO split on its RX lane tunables, so each is fed to both the -usb (USB3)
+ * and -cio (USB4) lane properties.
+ *
+ * NOT YET MAPPED - sub-block base unknown; left out rather than guessed, since a
+ * wrong base corrupts registers. SuperSpeed may still link without them; add
+ * once confirmed (macOS AppleT6050TypeCPhy): tunable_ATC0AXI2AF_LIOA,
+ * tunable_LN0/1_RX_CFG_TX_OF_RXCLK, tunable_UC_REGS_CIO_DFLT,
+ * tunable_LN0/1_RX_EQ_CIO_DFLT (the last two are empty in the J714c ADT).
+ */
+static const struct adt_tunable_info atc_tunables_t6050[] = {
+    /* global tunables applied after power on or reset */
+    {"tunable_ATC0AXI2AF", "apple,tunable-axi2af", 0x0, 0x8000, true},
+    {"tunable_ATC_FABRIC", "apple,tunable-common-b", 0x44000, 0x4000, true},
+    {"tunable_ATC_COMMON_CFG", "apple,tunable-common-b", 0x0, 0x4000, false},
+    {"tunable_AUS40CMN_SHM", "apple,tunable-common-b", 0xa00, 0x200, false},
+    {"tunable_AUSPLL_CORE", "apple,tunable-common-b", 0x2200, 0x4000, true},
+    {"tunable_CIO4PLL_CORE", "apple,tunable-common-b", 0x2a00, 0x200, false},
+    /* lane tunables - fed to both the USB3 (-usb) and USB4 (-cio) properties */
+    {"tunable_LN0_RX_TOP_CIO_DFLT", "apple,tunable-lane0-usb", 0x9000, 0x1000, true},
+    {"tunable_LN0_RX_TOP_CIO_DFLT", "apple,tunable-lane0-cio", 0x9000, 0x1000, true},
+    {"tunable_LN1_RX_TOP_CIO_DFLT", "apple,tunable-lane1-usb", 0x10000, 0x1000, true},
+    {"tunable_LN1_RX_TOP_CIO_DFLT", "apple,tunable-lane1-cio", 0x10000, 0x1000, true},
+    {"tunable_LN0_RX_EQ_DFLT", "apple,tunable-lane0-usb", 0xa000, 0x1000, false},
+    {"tunable_LN0_RX_EQ_DFLT", "apple,tunable-lane0-cio", 0xa000, 0x1000, false},
+    {"tunable_LN1_RX_EQ_DFLT", "apple,tunable-lane1-usb", 0x11000, 0x1000, false},
+    {"tunable_LN1_RX_EQ_DFLT", "apple,tunable-lane1-cio", 0x11000, 0x1000, false},
+};
